# Stage4 BASE package list — Libre Computer Le/La Frite (Amlogic arm64) LIGHT desktop
# One atom per line; lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This is the BASE (always-installed) set: kernel sources, u-boot tooling, the
# mesh/provisioning dependencies, and a hardened base system. The lean DESKTOP
# stack is a SEPARATE list (packages-light-desktop.list) appended by the builder
# when --desktop light (the default for this target) is selected, so the base can
# also produce a headless variant if ever needed.
#
# NOTE on the Amlogic boot chain (differs fundamentally from the RPi5 image):
#   * The Frite boots via mainline u-boot (libretech-ac / libretech-cc defconfig)
#     out of SPI NOR (La Frite) or microSD (Le Potato), then loads the kernel +
#     DTB + extlinux.conf from the first (FAT/ext) partition. There is NO
#     raspberrypi-firmware blob and NO config.txt.
#   * The board-specific DTB ships from the KERNEL build (gentoo-sources /
#     mainline), NOT from a vendor firmware package — see build-frite-stage4.sh
#     §"DTB". The u-boot binary itself is built/vendored by the builder (it needs
#     Amlogic's proprietary FIP/BL31 blobs to be flashable — see the script).

# ── Kernel sources (mainline; Amlogic GXL is fully upstream) ───────
# The S805X/S905X DTS are mainline since Linux 4.x/5.x. We build from
# gentoo-sources (vanilla + Gentoo patches) and select the in-tree
# arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-*.dtb at build time.
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources
sys-kernel/linux-firmware

# ── Bootloader tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# u-boot-tools provides mkimage (FIT/extlinux) used to assemble the boot blob;
# the actual u-boot binary for the board is built/fetched by the builder.
dev-embedded/u-boot-tools

# ── Board hardware / storage ──────────────────────────────────────
sys-block/parted
sys-apps/usbutils
sys-apps/i2c-tools
sys-apps/util-linux
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools

# ── Networking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
net-misc/networkmanager
net-misc/openssh
net-firewall/iptables
net-misc/socat
# WiFi supplicant is present so a USB WiFi dongle CAN work, but WiFi is OFF by
# default (hardened posture; the Frite has no onboard radio anyway — see
# harden_radios in the builder). Ethernet + the tailnet are the path.
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant

# ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
app-admin/sudo
sys-process/cronie
sys-apps/haveged
app-editors/nano
app-misc/screen
app-misc/jq

# ── Hardened / security (SELinux LSM) ──────────────────────────────
# Same posture as the cluster images: SELinux is the LSM. The policy packages'
# pkg_postinst runs the TARGET `semodule`, which can't execute under an aarch64
# cross-emerge — so the base policy is LOADED AT FIRST BOOT (native) by
# keys-provision (shared engine). See docs/SECURITY.md.
sec-policy/selinux-base
sec-policy/selinux-base-policy
sys-apps/policycoreutils
sys-apps/semodule-utils
sys-apps/checkpolicy
sys-libs/libselinux
sys-libs/libseccomp
sys-process/audit

# ── KEYS USB provisioning + attached storage ──────────────────────
# Same first-boot provisioning engine as every other client image: jq parses the
# manifests, dosfstools/util-linux handle the FAT32 KEYS partition + blkid.
net-fs/nfs-utils
net-fs/cifs-utils

# NOTE: headscale + tailscale are NOT emerged here. They are installed as
# upstream static arm64 binaries by build-frite-stage4.sh (the "mesh" phase),
# identical to the RPi5 image. See --skip-mesh / --skip-tailscale.
